---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const lastUpdated = '2026-04-03';
---

<Base title="Now" description="What I'm focused on right now.">
  <div class="container-sm">

    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="label"><span class="slash">// </span>MOD-04 — updated {lastUpdated}</p>
      <h1>Now<span style="color:var(--accent)">.</span></h1>
      <p class="page-desc">
        A <a href="https://nownownow.com" target="_blank">now page</a> — what I'm actually focused on,
        not what looks good. Updated at least once a month.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="now-sections">

      <section class="now-section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <span class="section-num">01</span>
          <h2>What I'm building</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="now-content">
          <p>This site, AXIOM.OS. I started it three weeks ago and it has already changed how I think about learning in public. The act of publishing forces clarity.</p>
          <p>Also tinkering with a CLI tool that auto-generates my weekly log entry by summarising commits, notes, and highlights from the week. Works about 70% of the time.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="now-section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <span class="section-num">02</span>
          <h2>What I'm learning</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="now-content">
          <div class="learning-list">
            <div class="learning-item">
              <span class="li-icon">📚</span>
              <div>
                <p class="li-title">Distributed Systems — Kleppmann's DDIA</p>
                <p class="li-note">Chapter 8: Trouble with distributed systems. The CAP theorem finally makes intuitive sense.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="learning-item">
              <span class="li-icon">🔧</span>
              <div>
                <p class="li-title">TypeScript — deep type system</p>
                <p class="li-note">Conditional types, infer keyword, template literal types. Genuinely powerful stuff.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="learning-item">
              <span class="li-icon">✍️</span>
              <div>
                <p class="li-title">Writing — daily practice</p>
                <p class="li-note">500 words every morning before opening email. Compounding faster than I expected.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="now-section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <span class="section-num">03</span>
          <h2>What I'm thinking about</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="now-content">
          <p>The tension between depth and breadth. Most advice says pick one — I think the best thinkers cycle between them deliberately.</p>
          <p>How to make a knowledge base that actually ages well. Most notes feel useless six months after writing them. I think the fix is connecting ideas, not filing them.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="now-section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <span class="section-num">04</span>
          <h2>Not doing</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="now-content">
          <p>Social media (mostly). Job hunting. Optimising this site before it has content. Starting new projects before finishing current ones.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="now-section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <span class="section-num">05</span>
          <h2>Where I am</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="now-content">
          <p>Parksville, British Columbia. Working remotely. If you're nearby and want to grab coffee and talk about distributed systems or personal knowledge management, reach out.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>

    <div class="now-footer">
      <p class="label"><span class="slash">// </span>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      <p class="now-footer-note">
        This is a <a href="https://nownownow.com/about" target="_blank">now page</a>.
        Inspired by Derek Sivers.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 60px 0 48px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-bottom: 60px;
  }
  .page-header .label { margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .page-desc {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .page-desc a { color: var(--accent2); }

  .now-sections { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; }

  .now-section {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 48px 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 48px;
  }

  .section-header { padding-top: 4px; }
  .section-num {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .now-section h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .now-content p {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #c0c8d0;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .now-content p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .learning-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px; }
  .learning-item { display: flex; gap: 16px; align-items: flex-start; }
  .li-icon { font-size: 18px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 2px; }
  .li-title {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .li-note { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }

  .now-footer {
    padding: 48px 0 40px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .now-footer-note { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
  .now-footer-note a { color: var(--accent2); }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .now-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  }
</style>
